Licences in this repository, per directory
==========================================

Everything that is code is GPL-2.0-or-later (full text: COPYING). Every source file carries
"SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later".

  loader/     GPL-2.0-or-later   a Linux kernel module (it is built against, and loaded into, WD's GPL-2.0
                                 kernel 3.2.40) and its emulator tests
  dts/        GPL-2.0-or-later   a device tree that includes Linux's own kirkwood .dtsi files
  userland/   GPL-2.0-or-later   ex4fan, ex4log, ex4peek, ex4phy: our own programs. GPL rather than MIT so that the whole
                                 tree has one licence and pieces can move into OpenWrt or the kernel tree
  box/        GPL-2.0-or-later   the script that runs on the NAS
  build/      GPL-2.0-or-later   the builders (mkoverlay.py patches two files of OpenWrt, which is GPL-2.0, at
                                 build time and carries shell hooks written against OpenWrt's function library)
  host/       GPL-2.0-or-later
  tests/      GPL-2.0-or-later   tests/captures/*.json are records of observed behaviour (bytes on a serial line);
                                 use them freely
  docs/, README.md, SAFETY.md    CC0 1.0 (public domain dedication,
                                 https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/): copy the protocol tables,
                                 pin maps and notes into any wiki, port or driver without asking

What is NOT in this repository, and why
---------------------------------------
No file of Western Digital's firmware (no binary, library, firmware image, root file system, U-Boot dump), and no
OpenWrt or Linux binary. build/fetch.sh downloads what is needed from the publishers themselves and checks hashes.
The protocol descriptions come from observing WD's programs; the code here is ours.

